## 3. Bug Life Cycle Diagram

```text
                         +----------------+
                         |      NEW       |
                         +----------------+
                                  |
                                  v
                         +----------------+
                         |    ASSIGNED    |
                         +----------------+
                                  |
                                  v
                         +----------------+
                         |      OPEN      |
                         +----------------+
                          /   |    |    \
                         /    |    |     \
                        v     v    v      v
                  +--------+ +------+ +----------+ +-------------+
                  |REJECTED| |FIXED | | DEFERRED | |  DUPLICATE  |
                  +--------+ +------+ +----------+ +-------------+
                       |        |
                       |        v
                       |   +----------+
                       |   |  RETEST  |
                       |   +----------+
                       |      |    |
                       |      |    +----------------+
                       |      |                     |
                       |      v                     v
                       | +----------+         +----------+
                       | | VERIFIED |         |   OPEN   |
                       | +----------+         +----------+
                       |      |
                       |      v
                       | +----------+
                       +>|  CLOSED  |
                         +----------+

        OPEN / NEW  --------->  NOT A BUG
```

**Main flow:**
**New → Assigned → Open → Fixed → Retest → Verified → Closed**

Other possible states from **Open** include: **Rejected, Deferred, Duplicate, or Not a Bug**. If the defect still exists during **Retest**, it is sent back to **Open**.

