## 4. Late Defect in a UPI Payment Feature

Suppose a defect is discovered after the Paytm app is live where a user's bank account is debited, but the payment status incorrectly shows **“Failed.”** The user may try to make the payment again, causing confusion and possible duplicate payments. Fixing this issue after release would require emergency development, testing, customer support, and possibly handling user complaints or refunds. If the defect had been found during development, it could have been fixed before release with much less cost and impact. Early detection would also protect user trust and avoid problems for many live users.
